<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heden II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 704–717</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Also known as Hedan II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heden II was a duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a> of the Hedenid line, based at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wurzburg">Würzburg</a> on the Main, in the early 8th century. He supported the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> missionary <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/willibrord">Willibrord</a>, granting him estates at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arnstadt">Arnstadt</a> in 704, and a church was founded on the Marienberg at Würzburg. After his rule the duchy came under direct Frankish control.</p></div>
